## Proposed Methods outline for review, 24 November 2026

**Historical proposal, subsequently agreed with reordered coverage; see resolution below.** Prepared from read-only inspection of the accepted evidence, provenance, saved results and implementing code. No producer, scoring, analysis or environment change was run. After agreement, save the outline in `paper_storyline.md` and its implementation/input/output/reproduction map in `evidence_and_sources.md`. Full section drafting remains with Issue 12.

**Working assumption and space tradeoff:** use six short subsections within the agreed 1.00-page Methods allowance. Preserve the exact approved three-paragraph sample description and complete H1 sensitivity passage. The sample description belongs in Methods; the full sensitivity motivation/result/qualification remains in Results, with its procedure in Methods. Coordinate display and validation definitions with the approved captions/table note. Keep exact paths, commands, hashes, recorded versions and fuller caveats in the repository map; do not assume a separate submitted supplement. Actual fit awaits compilation in Issues 13–14.

### 1. Study samples and provenance

**Purpose/detail:** explain the distinct units and eligibility using the exact approved sample wording. H1/network use 16,636 transfer events involving 4,602 players in recorded seasons 2012/13–2024/25. Guardian coverage uses 1,332 selected signings; main H2 retains 820, including 67 aged 30+. Age is completed years at transfer, grouped at 30. Explain H1's inherited club exclusions, real-club/non-PL origins and top-five-endpoint rule. Guardian selection uses July–June seasons, PL destinations from games, ages 18–36 and market value at least EUR 2m; exclude same-club moves and reversal of the immediately preceding move within 730 days unless a positive fee is recorded.

**Implementation/input/output:** [reduction manifest](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/provenance/reduction_manifest.json) and source-row records identify the [restricted transfer input](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/data/outsideprem_toprem_eligible_transfers.csv.gz). [`select()`](../../data/dataset_nlp/pipeline/get_guardian_articles.py) reads Transfermarkt transfers/players/games and writes [signings.csv](../../data/dataset_nlp/data/signings.csv). Use the [approved wording/audit](../evidence_and_sources.md#current-sample-description-for-review-21-november-2026).

**Limits:** separate event populations, not a shared cohort; different season conventions; repeated players; unverified completeness and original acquisition/version manifests. Reported Guardian fetch dates remain documentation claims.

### 2. Transfer network and selected backbone

**Purpose/detail:** provide structural context for Figure 1(a). Nodes are clubs; directed origin–destination routes are weighted by transfer count, pooling ages/seasons. Use saved directed weighted Louvain communities (resolution 1, optimizer seed 2026). For a route of weight `w`, eligible endpoints have degree `k > 1`, strength `s` and disparity score `(1-w/s)^(k-1)`, using outgoing quantities at the source and incoming quantities at the destination. Keep a route if either eligible score is strictly below 0.20. Degree-one endpoints have no score; the producer's connectivity exception has zero cases in the selected whole-network view. H1 uses the full sample.

**Implementation/input/output:** [restricted backbone producer](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/notebooks/louvain_transfer_backbone.py), saved route graph and Louvain membership; `backbone_route_scores.csv`, `backbone_retention.csv`, `backbone_layout.csv` and `backbone_results.json` in restricted `output/louvain_transfer_backbone_findings/`. The [Figure 1 map](../../output/backbone_h1_findings/README.md) traces the frozen layout and selected view.

**Limits:** exploratory local filter, not an age test. The selected whole-network R comparison agrees; retain the separate within-community floating-point discrepancy and unverified historical browser interaction in provenance. Use Issue 07's selected Louvain/directed-modularity and disparity references.

### 3. H1 entry-rate test and fixed-player sensitivity

**Purpose/detail:** define the older-minus-younger PL joining-rate gap in percentage points, using all eligible events in each age denominator. Shuffle age labels 999 times within origin club and recorded season, fixing outcomes and stratum age counts. Use `p=(1+count(shuffled gap <= observed gap))/1000`, including ties. Seed 2026 supplies separate streams for main shuffles, selection and sensitivity shuffles. Uniformly select one eligible event per player once without selecting on age/destination; hold the 4,602 selected events fixed for sensitivity permutations.

**Implementation/input/output:** [H1 producer](../../notebooks/age_shuffle_outsideprem_toprem.py), restricted input and season-specific league lookup; [results JSON](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/output/age_shuffle_outsideprem_toprem_results.json), summary, [independent verification](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/provenance/h1_verification.json) and [fixed-player membership](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/provenance/h1_sensitivity_selected_rows.csv).

**Limits:** within-stratum exchangeability is assumed; the conditional null need not centre on zero. Repeated players threaten that assumption. The sensitivity changes weighting and conditions on one draw, without assessing alternative selections. The illustrative normal curve and shuffle SD are not confidence intervals. Use the agreed permutation/dependence references without implying that a multilevel dependence-preserving procedure was implemented.

### 4. Guardian sentence measurement and validation

**Purpose/detail:** explain the football API name-variant search over ±365 days, sentence/name matching and ambiguity screens, plus a following He/His sentence without its own player-name match. Same-player article links go to the nearest signing; different players can share articles. Score with CardiffNLP `twitter-roberta-base-sentiment-latest` as `P(positive)-P(negative)` (128-token truncation), VADER compound, Bing's positive-minus-negative lexicon balance divided by their total (zero when no matches), and Bing excluding the listed 21 football words. Main H2 retains quotes/passing mentions and applies no focus-only filter.

One author labelled 200 sentences; exclude four wrong-person cases from validation. Define Spearman rank agreement on 196 ordered human labels, sign agreement on 85 polar labels, and three-class accuracy on all 196. Neutral thresholds are inclusive ±0.05 for RoBERTa/VADER and exactly zero for Bing. Rank-correlation intervals use 2,000 sentence bootstrap resamples, 2.5th/97.5th percentiles (seed 2805). Coordinate with Table 1's note rather than repeating its Results interpretation.

**Implementation/input/output:** [collection/build code](../../data/dataset_nlp/pipeline/get_guardian_articles.py), [pipeline spec](../../data/dataset_nlp/pipeline/pipeline_spec.yaml), [scorers](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_sentiment.py) and [validation code](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/b9_score.py); inputs are signings, articles, sentences, full scores and human labels. Saved validation outputs in NLP `results/` are `b9_labels_joined.csv`, `b9_model_scores.csv` and `b9_confusion.csv`.

**Limits:** whole-sentence tone can concern another target or speaker. Only 14 evaluated sentences concern older players. Historical label sampling/blinding and annotator agreement are not independently established. Raw text/full scores/caches are missing; the model identifier alone does not establish a frozen historical revision. Use the selected API/instrument/checkpoint citations, separating theory from project implementation.

### 5. H2 comparison and monthly display

**Purpose/detail:** exclude liveblogs/match reports, use days −365 to −8 and +8 to +365, and require at least five scored sentences on each side. Average within each signing-period, calculate after-minus-before, then compare mean changes by age with equal signing weight. Shuffle age labels 5,000 times within signing season (seed 2805); use `p=(1+count(|shuffled gap| >= |observed gap|))/5001`.

For the display, average within signing-month and then across contributing signings. Bins use `floor(days/30.44)`, clipped to −12…11. Smooth with a centred three-month moving average separately before/after, allowing two months at endpoints. Monthly membership varies. Period-mean dots are separate calculations; their short segments are fixed display markers. No uncertainty intervals are shown; omit the historical unverified H2 gap interval.

**Implementation/input/output:** [`per_signing()`](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_sentiment.py), [H2 test](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_age30.py), [monthly producer](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_age30_arc.py); NLP `results/a1_age30_results.csv`, `a1_age30_levels.csv` and model-specific per-signing files; four-model `figures/plotting/data/a1_h2_arc_4models.csv`. The [Figure 2 map](../../output/h2_monthly_period_means_findings/README.md) records selectors/export provenance.

**Limits:** within-season exchangeability remains an assumption; repeated signings/shared articles and unequal coverage retention limit inference. Bing curves have documented saved-export provenance without independent regeneration from original sentence caches. Curves and tone levels do not themselves test differences in changes.

### 6. Descriptive coverage and reproducibility

**Purpose/detail:** count distinct article IDs with at least one coded player-name mention per signing-period over the same day windows, with all article types and all 1,332 selected signings. Reindex to all signing IDs and fill missing counts with zero before calculating age-group medians separately before/after. Do not include historical coverage regressions or H2b adjustment/quote-removal procedures.

**Implementation/input/output:** [`counts()` and median construction](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_coverage_age.py), [text-free metadata](../../data/dataset_nlp/data/article_player_notext.csv.gz) and signings; saved `a1_coverage_age.csv` all-article-types before/after median fields and `signing_tone.csv` counts. Link the [restricted execution log](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/provenance/run_log.md), hashes and recorded versions/commands; do not imply one historical environment for all analyses.

**Limits:** derived tables, code, labels and article metadata are available. Original acquisition manifests, article bodies, original sentences, full scores and caches are unavailable at documented paths, preventing complete historical Guardian reconstruction. Do not repeat the NLP README's unconditional rebuild claim. Issue 9.1 remains deferred and contributes no completed corpus analysis or Methods subsection.

**Next review:** agree the six purposes and level of detail, then save the agreed outline/map in the planning files. Known source/dependence gaps stay explicit limitations. No new analysis or manuscript inclusion is proposed. The full source map above is planning material, not proposed one-page manuscript prose.

